s8-6-p13 : Block
s8-6-p13 = prose (cons "This classification is also the boundary for a Clang-based lift. An elaborated AST, together with its preprocessing context, selected overloads, instantiated templates, and source locations, is a derivation-shaped object for *some* static judgments. Importing it into \(\mathsf{StdDeriv}\) requires a stated translation and evidence that each imported elaboration decision satisfies the selected source-rule instances. The translation is an explicit frontend assumption until established; it is not automatically the inverse map \(g\) of (5.13), which concerns an already selected formal signature. Proving that the actual frontend constructs only admitted elaborations would discharge that assumption for its specified input domain. A complete C++ fidelity claim additionally covers dynamic semantics and the external prose-to-rule correspondence; frontend soundness alone does not establish those." nil)
